## Run it

{% if has_compose %}
### With Docker (everything in one command)

```bash
cp .env.example .env      # then add your API key(s)
docker compose up --build
```

{% if has_ui %}Open http://localhost:{{ deploy.frontend_port }} for the chat, or {% endif %}http://localhost:{{ deploy.backend_port }}/docs for the API.

{% endif %}
### Locally

Needs Python 3.12+{% if has_ui %} and Node.js 20+{% endif %}.

```bash
make setup      # creates .env, installs dependencies
make test       # runs the test suite offline, no API key needed
make dev        # API on :8000{% if has_ui %}, chat UI on :{{ deploy.frontend_port }}{% endif %}

```

### Try it without an API key

Set `LLM_PROVIDER=fake` in `.env`. Every step answers with a placeholder, so you can
click through the whole flow{% if has_approval %}, including approvals{% endif %}, without spending anything.
{% if has_rag %}

